WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.480
There are legends in basketball so famous, you&nbsp;
know them by one name. Jordan, kobe, Lebron,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:12.480
and there is a legend who is status is so iconic,&nbsp;
you know him by one letter, K, as in coach K. For&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:17.880
42 seasons, Mike krzyzewski served as the&nbsp;
head coach for the duke blue devils. He won&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:27.680
five national championships before retiring. I sat&nbsp;
down with him to talk about life, coaching wisdom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:38.228
and what is more important than winning.
&gt;&gt; It's a pretty cool view.&nbsp;

00:00:38.228 --> 00:00:42.317
&gt;&gt; Yeah.
&gt;&gt; And you know, all the banners and --&nbsp;

00:00:42.317 --> 00:00:44.560
&gt;&gt; That's all your national championships.
&gt;&gt; The five, yeah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:52.000
and final fours and ACC championships.
&gt;&gt; You're often described by people in profiles of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.595
you as the son of a cleaning woman and an elevator&nbsp;
operator. But I don't think that's how you

00:00:57.595 --> 00:00:57.607
[8:44:26 AM]

00:00:57.607 --> 00:00:59.660
But I don't think that's how&nbsp;
you would describe your parents.&nbsp;

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:05.520
&gt;&gt; No, my parents were the basis of who me and&nbsp;
my brother became. They taught us the dignity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:13.840
of work, I even tell my teams for years, I want&nbsp;
you to be as tough as your mother. And just think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:20.200
about your mother, was there ever a day that she&nbsp;
didn't show up? Did you ever see her sick? Did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:26.720
you ever see her tired? I never saw my mom sick&nbsp;
or tired. I saw her every day doing everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:33.440
that she could possibly do to make it nice for&nbsp;
me and my brother, bill. I didn't appreciate it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:40.360
until later in life. And my dad died when I was&nbsp;
a senior at west point. He didn't go by the name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:47.080
krzyzewski, he went by the name "Cross." He was&nbsp;
always afraid of losing his job because there was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:53.477
a lot of ethnic discrimination at that time. I&nbsp;
didn't realize all the things that my parents --&nbsp;

00:01:53.477 --> 00:01:55.820
&gt;&gt; Gave up?
&gt;&gt; Gave up. &gt;&gt; Hid?

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:55.832
[8:45:27 AM]

00:01:55.832 --> 00:01:59.840
&gt;&gt; Hid? Your parents didn't even want&nbsp;
you guys to learn to speak Polish.&nbsp;

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:02.180
&gt;&gt; Polish, right.
&gt;&gt; Why?&nbsp;

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:07.480
&gt;&gt; And I didn't find out this until later,&nbsp;
they didn't want us to have an accent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:13.960
because they were afraid again -- they're&nbsp;
in that time, somebody with a vowel at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:17.700
end of their name may have been looked&nbsp;
at differently. They were concerned.&nbsp;

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:20.120
&gt;&gt; They were trying to protect you.
&gt;&gt; They were trying to protect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:21.920
me and my brother.
&gt;&gt; So much so that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:26.200
wasn't on his tombstone until --
&gt;&gt; Yeah. He was in World War II as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:32.520
William cross. And so when he died, and we, you&nbsp;
know, were a low-income family, the government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:38.200
provides a tombstone. It said "Cross." And we&nbsp;
weren't able to change that until my mom passed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:45.480
and my brother and I made sure it said krzyzewski.&nbsp;
I was fortunate to be inducted into the basketball&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:53.120
hall of fame in 2001 and one of the parts of the&nbsp;
speech and probably the most emotional for me was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:57.358
I said, I wish my mom and dad were&nbsp;
here tonight -- I'm going to start

00:02:57.358 --> 00:02:57.370
[8:46:27 AM]

00:02:57.370 --> 00:03:03.640
tonight -- I'm going to start crying, to see&nbsp;
a krzyzewski go into the hall of flame. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:11.240
was emotional then, it's emotional now, because I&nbsp;
recognized just the life they led to make sure me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:17.360
and bill would be taken care of. Amazing.
&gt;&gt; How much of what you've done and how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:21.480
you've led and carried on this&nbsp;
name so proudly, it's so famous.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:26.360
I just walked in the krzyzewski center.
&gt;&gt; They couldn't find another name for it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:31.280
so they put one that no one could pronounce.
&gt;&gt; I love this picture.&nbsp;

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:34.240
&gt;&gt; Yeah. You can tell she's --
&gt;&gt; Proud.&nbsp;

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:37.600
&gt;&gt; Proud.
&gt;&gt; I've been married 53 years to Becky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:43.840
and we knew that it was going to be a partnership.&nbsp;
I call it, two is better than one if two can act&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:51.880
as one. And we were able to act as one. That's&nbsp;
my family. Whenever we played in the olympics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.708
we brought everybody.
&gt;&gt; You did?&nbsp;

00:03:53.708 --> 00:03:55.200
&gt;&gt; Yeah.
&gt;&gt; You did a lot of it all together.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.120
[8:47:28 AM]

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:57.260
together.
&gt;&gt; I have three daughters.&nbsp;

00:03:57.260 --> 00:04:02.480
&gt;&gt; They hold you down to Earth?
&gt;&gt; They -- whatever humility I did not have,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:09.800
they try to interject over and over, so when&nbsp;
there used to be family dinners and people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:15.680
